From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jfacemyer <1776340+jfacemyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:31:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wintab32: Drop the oldest packet, not the newest,
 when a context queue overflows.

On overflow AddPacketToContextQueue() discarded the incoming packet and
flagged the last queued one, yet the caller still posted WT_PACKET with
the discarded packet's serial number, which WTPacket() then could not
find. An application that drains the queue slowly kept reading stale
positions (the proximity entry point at pen-down time) while the fresh
contact packets were thrown away, which draws a stray line.

Now the oldest packet is dropped and the new one is queued with
TPS_QUEUE_ERR set. The overflow test also catches a queue left longer
than its size by WTQueueSizeSet(), and a zero-sized queue no longer
writes before the start of the buffer.

From neutron-wine (Nico-LaFoucate), the wintab32 part of its
neutron-wintab patch.
---
 dlls/wintab32/context.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/wintab32/context.c b/dlls/wintab32/context.c
index e730477..7ee762f 100644
--- a/dlls/wintab32/context.c
+++ b/dlls/wintab32/context.c
@@ -232,25 +232,30 @@ LPOPENCONTEXT AddPacketToContextQueue(LPWTPACKET packet, HWND hwnd)
 
             DUMPPACKET(*packet);
 
-            if (tgt == ptr->QueueSize)
+            if (tgt >= ptr->QueueSize)
             {
-                TRACE("Queue Overflow %p\n",ptr->handle);
-                ptr->PacketQueue[tgt-1].pkStatus |= TPS_QUEUE_ERR;
+                /* Drop the oldest packet, not this one: the caller posts WT_PACKET
+                 * with this packet's serial number, and the application must find
+                 * the newest position in the queue, not a stale one. */
+                TRACE("Queue Overflow %p, dropping the oldest packet\n",ptr->handle);
+                if (ptr->QueueSize <= 0) break;
+                tgt = ptr->QueueSize - 1;
+                memmove(ptr->PacketQueue, &ptr->PacketQueue[1], tgt * sizeof(WTPACKET));
+                ptr->PacketsQueued = tgt;
+                packet->pkStatus |= TPS_QUEUE_ERR;
             }
-            else
+
+            TRACE("Placed in queue %p index %i\n",ptr->handle,tgt);
+            ptr->PacketQueue[tgt] = *packet;
+            ptr->PacketsQueued++;
+
+            if (ptr->ActiveCursor != packet->pkCursor)
             {
-                TRACE("Placed in queue %p index %i\n",ptr->handle,tgt);
-                ptr->PacketQueue[tgt] = *packet;
-                ptr->PacketsQueued++;
-
-                if (ptr->ActiveCursor != packet->pkCursor)
-                {
-                    ptr->ActiveCursor = packet->pkCursor;
-                    if (ptr->context.lcOptions & CXO_CSRMESSAGES)
-                        TABLET_PostTabletMessage(ptr, _WT_CSRCHANGE(ptr->context.lcMsgBase),
-                          (WPARAM)packet->pkSerialNumber, (LPARAM)ptr->handle,
-                            FALSE);
-                }
+                ptr->ActiveCursor = packet->pkCursor;
+                if (ptr->context.lcOptions & CXO_CSRMESSAGES)
+                    TABLET_PostTabletMessage(ptr, _WT_CSRCHANGE(ptr->context.lcMsgBase),
+                      (WPARAM)packet->pkSerialNumber, (LPARAM)ptr->handle,
+                        FALSE);
             }
             break;
          }
